            <ArticleTitle>Unusual complications of coronary artery bypass graft surgery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1665-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Complications after coronary artery bypass grafting are myriad and are to a certain extent operator dependent. The investigators report 2 unusual cases of inadvertent aortocoronary fistula after coronary artery bypass grafting that escaped routine detection. In conclusion, the development of heart failure led to the detection of this rare complication.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
